Subject: [PATCH] display: let the host choose the guest's boot resolution and refresh rate

Two choices, read like REIMS_VGPU_RAIL:

  - REIMS_VGPU_DISPLAY_MODE = 1920x1080 | 1600x900 | 1280x720 | 960x540
    puts that 16:9 mode first in the timing elements (element 0 is what the
    guest boots at), followed by the smaller 16:9 modes and no larger one: a
    guest restores a larger mode it ran at before whenever it is offered.
    Only 16:9 because the announced panel is.
  - REIMS_VGPU_DISPLAY_HZ = 120 | 60 | 30
    goes into every timing element and paces the VBL limiter, so the rate the
    guest reads and the interrupt it is woken by stay one number.

Unset, both keep today's behaviour. Adopted or refused, each is reported
once on the failure channel. For an iOS host, where the guest's compositor
runs on emulated cores and 1920x1080 at 120 Hz is far past what it can keep.

diff --git a/crates/reims-vgpu-config/src/lib.rs b/crates/reims-vgpu-config/src/lib.rs
index a60d4181..571bb9cb 100644
--- a/crates/reims-vgpu-config/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/reims-vgpu-config/src/lib.rs
@@ -1241,6 +1241,39 @@ choices! {
 /// changed" ambiguous between "the build does not carry that rail" and "the
 /// device declined the ask".
 pub const RAIL: &str = "REIMS_VGPU_RAIL";
+
+/// **A choice, not a switch.** Which resolution the guest's display boots at.
+///
+/// Accepted values are the 16:9 modes spelled `WIDTHxHEIGHT` — `1920x1080`,
+/// `1600x900`, `1280x720`, `960x540`. The named mode becomes timing element 0,
+/// which the guest takes as its native and preferred mode, and the smaller 16:9
+/// modes follow it. No larger one is offered: a guest that ran at a larger mode
+/// before restores it whenever it is on the list.
+///
+/// Only 16:9, because the announced panel is 16:9: a mode of another aspect
+/// would tell the guest its pixels are not square. Only modes no larger than the
+/// default native one, because the reason to ask is a host that cannot keep up
+/// with 1920x1080 — every pixel the guest composites is one the host renders.
+///
+/// Unset keeps the default list — 1920x1080 first, then 1440x1080, 1280x1024
+/// and 3840x2160 — unchanged. A value outside the list is refused on the
+/// failure channel and the default list is offered.
+pub const DISPLAY_MODE: &str = "REIMS_VGPU_DISPLAY_MODE";
+
+/// **A choice, not a switch.** The refresh rate the guest's display runs at.
+///
+/// Accepted values are `120`, `60` and `30`. The rate goes into every timing
+/// element the guest reads, and the VBL interrupt the guest is woken by is paced
+/// to match — the two always agree, because the guest honours the interrupt and
+/// a table that said otherwise would be a lie it never notices.
+///
+/// It exists for a host that cannot emulate the guest's compositor at 120 Hz:
+/// macOS paces CoreAnimation to the display, so a slower display is less work
+/// per second for every emulated core, and fewer interrupts besides.
+///
+/// Unset is 120 Hz, as before. A value outside the list is refused on the
+/// failure channel and 120 Hz is used.
+pub const DISPLAY_HZ: &str = "REIMS_VGPU_DISPLAY_HZ";
 }
 
 /// What one variable says, including the two ways it says nothing usable.
